      "candidate": "mathcomp finset [set:: s]",
      "note": "MathComp's [set:: s] (finset.v; set_nil, set_seq1, set_cons) is the support of an arbitrary sequence; GTBase.walks_paths.seq_vertices names it and adds the lemma API. coq-graph-theory has no name for the vertex set of a raw sequence: GraphTheory.digraph.nodes is locked (x :: val p) on a packaged Path x y only, so it is never empty and requires a pathp proof, and the library writes the vertex set of a packaged path as [set z in p]. The local helpers take raw sequences without any walk, uniqueness or nonemptiness premise, so nodes is not a faithful canonical; seq_vertices_nodes and seq_vertices_val state the exact correspondence, and X2's head-plus-tail helper is seq_vertices (x :: s). All nine helpers are convertible to the canonical; Legacy bodies and per-row certificates: meta/migration_reports/path_vertices.md.",
